<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14055" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Dĭŏgĕnes</span></b> ,
			is, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Διογένης</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Apolloniates, <i>a celebrated Ionian philosopher, pupil
				of Anaximenes</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 1, 12,
			29</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>The well-known Cynic philosopher of Sinope</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic. Tusc. 1, 43, 104</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. N. D. 3,
				34</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Mur. 36</span></i> et
			saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Stoic, teacher of Carneades and Laelius</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Cic.
				Div. 1, 3, 6</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Fin. 2, 8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 4,
			3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de Sen. 7</span></i> et
			saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A friend of M. Caelius Rufus</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				2, 12, 2</span></i>; id. Cael. <i><span class="en">ib. 8, 8,
			10</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>